==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|it|en}} {{term|grotta|lang=it}}, from {{etyl|VL.|en}} {{term|grupta}}, from Classical {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|crypta|lang=la}}; see {{term|crypt}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|British}} {{IPA|/ˈɡɹɒt.əʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈɡɹɑ.toʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-grotto.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɒtəʊ|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|s|grottoes}}

# A small [[cave]].
# An [[artificial]] [[cavern-like]] [[retreat]].
# A [[Marian]] [[shrine]], usually built in a cavern-like structure.

